  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improvement of Bor State Hospital Service Delivery through 50 Kwh Solarization Plant with Battery Bank</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bor State Hospital (BSH) is the primary health care facility in Bor, supporting the town&apos;s population of 100,000 persons, as well as the population of the five surrounding counties within Jonglei state, the Awerial County (Mingkaman) of Lakes State, and the northern area of Central Equatoria state. The hospital currently relies on four generators, but the solar power system in use is unreliable for supporting the increasing needs of the hospital. Based on current needs, a regular power supply would allow Bor Hospital to provide more reliable and safe services. It would significantly reduce the daily carbon dioxide emissions and enable the hospital to provide select services during the night, a service currently not available. 
 
Through this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is improving the capacity of BSH to provide healthcare services to flood-affected and vulnerable communities in Bor State and the surrounding areas. This is achieved through the provision of reliable and green energy, through the installation of a solar panel system and battery bank as well as training for BSH staff on the operation and maintenance of the new system.</narrative>
  </description>
